nvolved in studies on dietary management of irritable bowel syndrome."}{"title": "CHUMPITAZI BP:Chumpitazi BP is a researcher who has studied dietary carbohydrates and their effects on childhood abdominal pain."}{"title": "SHULMAN RJ:Shulman RJ is a researcher focused on dietary treatments for gastrointestinal issues in children."}{"title": "HASKA L:Haska L is a researcher who has studied fructan metabolism in cereals."}{"title": "NYMAN M:Nyman M is a researcher involved in studies on dietary fiber and its effects on health."}{"title": "ANDERSSON R:Andersson R is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dietary fiber components."}{"title": "KARPPINEN S:Karppinen S is a researcher focused on the fructan content of rye and its products."}{"title": "MYLLYM\u00c4KI O:Myllym\u00e4ki O is a researcher involved in studies on cereal chemistry."}{"title": "FORSELL P:Forssell P is a researcher who has studied the properties of rye and its nutritional components."}{"title": "POUTANEN K:Poutanen K is a researcher focused on the health implications of dietary fibers."}{"title": "HUYNH BL:Huynh BL is a researcher who has studied the effects of grain on health."}{"title": "PALMER L:Palmer L is a researcher involved in studies on the nutritional aspects of grains."}{"title": "MATHER DE:Mather DE is a researcher who has contributed to studies on grain science."}{"title": "WALLWORK H:Wallwork H is a researcher focused on the nutritional value of grains."}{"title": "GRAHAM RD:Graham RD is a researcher who has studied the mineral content of grains and its health implications."}{"title": "WELCH RM:Welch RM is a researcher involved in studies on the nutritional aspects of food sources."}{"title": "STANGOULIS JCR:Stangoulis JCR is a researcher who has studied the health benefits of grains."}{"title": "VIETOR RJ:Vietor RJ is a researcher focused on the polysaccharide content in grains."}{"title": "VORAGEN AGJ:Voragen AGJ is a researcher who has contributed to studies on non-starch polysaccharides."}{"title": "ANGELINO S:Angelino S is a researcher involved in studies on grain processing and its nutritional implications."}{"title": "PILNIK W:Pilnik W is a researcher who has studied the effects of grain processing on health."}{"title": "AM J GASTROENTEROL:The American Journal of Gastroenterology, abbreviated as AM J GASTROENTEROL, is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on gastrointestinal health. It covers a wide range of topics related to gastrointestinal diseases, including significant studies on nutrition in acute pancreatitis. The journal serves as a vital resource for researchers and healthcare professionals in the field of gastroenterology, contributing to the advancement of knowledge and treatment options for gastrointestinal conditions."}{"title": "ALIMENT PHARMACOL THER:Alimentary Pharmacology & Therapeutics, a journal that publishes research on gastrointestinal pharmacology and nutrition."}{"title": "MAP DIET:The MAP diet is a dietary approach used for the treatment of irritable bowel syndrome, focusing on specific carbohydrate intake to alleviate symptoms."}{"title": "GASTROENTEROLOGY AND HEPATOLOGY:Gastroenterology and Hepatology is a medical journal that publishes research related to gastrointestinal and liver diseases."}{"title": "ANNALS OF NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:Annals of Nutrition and Metabolism is a journal that focuses on the nutritional aspects of health and disease."}{"title": "CLINICAL GASTROENTEROLOGY AND HEPATOLOGY:Clinical Gastroenterology and Hepatology is a journal dedicated to the dissemination of clinical research and information pertaining to the fields of gastroenterology and hepatology. It emphasizes the clinical aspects of these medical specialties, providing valuable insights and findings that contribute to the understanding and treatment of gastrointestinal and liver diseases."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF NEUROGASTROENTEROLOGY AND MOTILITY:Journal of Neurogastroenterology and Motility focuses on the study of gastrointestinal motility and related disorders."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF HUMAN NUTRITION AND DIETETICS:Journal of Human Nutrition and Dietetics publishes research on human nutrition and dietary practices."}{"title": "NUTRITION JOURNAL:Nutrition Journal is a peer-reviewed journal that covers all aspects of nutrition science."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CROHN'S AND COLITIS:Journal of Crohn's and Colitis publishes research on inflammatory bowel diseases, including Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis."}{"title": "NUTR CLIN MED:Nutr Clin Med is a journal that discusses clinical nutrition and its impact on health."}{"title": "DR. PEDRO PABLO GARC\u00cdA LUNA:Dr. Pedro Pablo Garc\u00eda Luna is a medical professional involved in nutritional support for patients with renal insufficiency."}{"title": "DR. LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO:Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo is a medical professional who specializes in nutritional support for patients with renal conditions."}{"title": "DRES. MERCEDES V\u00c1ZQUEZ GUTI\u00c9RREZ:Dra. Mercedes V\u00e1zquez Guti\u00e9rrez is a medical professional focusing on nutritional support in chronic liver disease and liver transplantation."}{"title": "JUAN PEDRO RODR\u00cdGUEZ RODR\u00cdGUEZ:Dr. Juan Pedro Rodr\u00edguez Rodr\u00edguez is a resident in internal medicine at Hospital de Poniente in El Ejido, Almer\u00eda. He specializes in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic conditions, specifically focusing on renal patients and those suffering from chronic liver disease. His work emphasizes the importance of tailored nutritional interventions to improve the health outcomes of these vulnerable patient populations."}{"title": "IRRITABLE BOWEL SYNDROME:Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) is a common gastrointestinal disorder that affects the large intestine. It is characterized by a range of symptoms including abdominal pain, cramping, bloating, gas, and altered bowel habits, which may manifest as diarrhea or constipation. Additionally, IBS can be associated with various food intolerances, further complicating the management of the condition."}{"title": "DIET THERAPY:Diet therapy involves the use of specific dietary practices to manage health conditions, including inflammatory bowel diseases and irritable bowel syndrome."}{"title": "CIDOS:CIDOS is an organization involved in nutritional support and medical education related to renal insufficiency and other health topics."}{"title": "PEDRO PABLO GARC\u00cdA LUNA:Dr. Pedro Pablo Garc\u00eda Luna is a medical professional associated with CIDOS, focusing on nutritional support in renal insufficiency."}{"title": "LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO:Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo is a medical professional associated with CIDOS, focusing on nutritional support in renal insufficiency."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA DEL PILAR SERRANO AGUAYO:Dr. Mar\u00eda del Pilar Serrano Aguayo is a medical professional specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition. She is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation. Dr. Serrano Aguayo works at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc\u00edo in Sevilla, where she applies her expertise to enhance the health and well-being of her patients."}{"title": "JOS\u00c9 MANUEL SOUSA MART\u00cdN:Dr. Jos\u00e9 Manuel Sousa Mart\u00edn is a medical professional specializing in the Digestive System, particularly within the Hepatic Transplant Unit at Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc\u00edo in Sevilla. He is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation."}{"title": "CARMEN SENDRA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Carmen Sendra Fern\u00e1ndez is a Resident Physician specializing in the Digestive System at the Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc\u00edo in Sevilla. In her role, Dr. Sendra Fern\u00e1ndez is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care in this critical area of medicine."}{"title": "ANA M. G\u00d3MEZ P\u00c9REZ:Ana M. G\u00f3mez P\u00e9rez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quir\u00f3n-salud in M\u00e1laga. She is a medical professional who focuses on nutritional support for celiac disease and gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in managing dietary needs related to these conditions."}{"title": "ROSARIO FERN\u00c1NDEZ GARC\u00cdA-SALAZAR:Dr. Rosario Fern\u00e1ndez Garc\u00eda-Salazar is a medical professional specializing in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quir\u00f3n-salud in M\u00e1laga. She is particularly involved in providing nutritional support for celiac disease and managing gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in addressing dietary needs related to these conditions."}{"title": "LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO P\u00c9REZ:Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo P\u00e9rez is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders and is actively involved in research and practice related to nutritional support in metabolic disorders. He is associated with the Unidad de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica at Hospital Universitario Infanta Cristina, where he focuses on clinical nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "ANA M. M\u00c1RQUEZ ARMENTEROS:Dr. Ana M. M\u00e1rquez Armenteros is a medical professional involved in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders."}{"title": "PILAR JIM\u00c9NEZ NACIMIENTO:Dr. Pilar Jim\u00e9nez Nacimiento is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders. She is affiliated with the Departamento de Ciencias Biom\u00e9dicas at the Universidad de Extremadura, where she contributes to the field of biomedical sciences."}{"title": "HOSPITAL DE PONIENTE:Hospital de Poniente is a medical facility located in El Ejido, Almer\u00eda, where Dr. Juan Pedro Rodr\u00edguez Rodr\u00edguez is a resident in internal medicine."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CELIACA:Celiac disease, known as \"enfermedad cel\u00edaca,\" is a chronic autoimmune disorder that primarily affects the small intestine. It is triggered by the ingestion of gluten in genetically predisposed individuals, leading to inflammation and damage to the intestinal mucosa. This condition results in malabsorption of nutrients, which can manifest through various gastrointestinal and extraintestinal symptoms. \n\nCeliac disease is characterized by the atrophy of the intestinal villi, particularly impacting nutrient absorption, especially in children. To manage the disease and prevent adverse reactions, individuals diagnosed with celiac disease must adhere to a strict gluten-free diet. This dietary restriction is essential to avoid further damage to the small intestine and to correct nutritional deficiencies that may arise from the condition. Overall, celiac disease is a significant health concern that requires careful management and lifestyle adjustments to ensure the well-being of affected individuals."}{"title": "METABOLISMOS DE LOS AMINO\u00c1CIDOS:Amino acid metabolism disorders involve the body's inability to properly process amino acids, requiring specialized nutritional support."}{"title": "HOSPITAL TORREC\u00c1RDENAS:"}{"title": "SOCIETY INTERNACIONAL DE NUTRICI\u00d3N Y METABOLISMO RENAL:The International Society of Renal Nutrition and Metabolism (ISRNM) is an organization that establishes guidelines and consensus on nutritional support for patients with kidney disease."}{"title": "PEW:Protein-energy wasting (PEW) is a syndrome characterized by the loss of body protein mass and energy reserves in chronic kidney disease patients, leading to malnutrition."}{"title": "HIPERFOSFATEMIA:Hiperfosfatemia is a condition characterized by elevated phosphate levels in the blood, often associated with kidney dysfunction."}{"title": "OSTEODISTROFIA RENAL:Osteodistrofia renal, also known as renal osteodystrophy, is a bone disorder that arises in patients suffering from chronic kidney disease. This condition is primarily caused by imbalances in calcium, phosphate, and vitamin D levels, which are critical for maintaining healthy bone structure. Renal osteodystrophy is recognized as a complication of chronic kidney disease and is often associated with issues related to phosphorus metabolism. As a result, patients with chronic kidney disease may experience significant alterations in their bone health due to these metabolic disturbances."}{"title": "BICARBONATOS:"}{"title": "CITOQUINAS PROINFLAMATORIAS:Citoquinas proinflamatorias son prote\u00ednas que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la modulaci\u00f3n de la respuesta inmune. Estas mol\u00e9culas de se\u00f1alizaci\u00f3n se encuentran elevadas en pacientes con insuficiencia renal cr\u00f3nica, lo que contribuye a la inflamaci\u00f3n y malnutrici\u00f3n en estos individuos. Adem\u00e1s, las citoquinas proinflamatorias aumentan durante episodios de inflamaci\u00f3n, lo que puede afectar negativamente la salud de pacientes en estado cr\u00edtico. En resumen, las citoquinas proinflamatorias son fundamentales en la regulaci\u00f3n de la respuesta inmune y tienen un impacto significativo en la salud de aquellos que padecen condiciones cr\u00edticas y enfermedades cr\u00f3nicas."}{"title": "HIPOALDOSTERONISMO HIPERRENIN\u00c9MICO:El hiperaldosteronismo hiperrenin\u00e9mico es una condici\u00f3n que se presenta en el s\u00edndrome nefr\u00f3tico, causando retenci\u00f3n de agua y sodio."}{"title": "DIETISTAS:Los dietistas son expertos en nutrici\u00f3n que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la planificaci\u00f3n y evaluaci\u00f3n de la ingesta diet\u00e9tica de los pacientes, especialmente en contextos de nutrici\u00f3n enteral. Estos profesionales de la salud est\u00e1n especializados en ayudar a los pacientes a mantener una dieta adecuada, lo cual es particularmente importante en condiciones m\u00e9dicas como la insuficiencia renal. Adem\u00e1s, los dietistas son responsables de la planificaci\u00f3n y supervisi\u00f3n de la nutrici\u00f3n de los pacientes, asegurando que sus necesidades diet\u00e9ticas sean atendidas de manera efectiva y personalizada."}{"title": "NFK-DOQI:NFK-DOQI es una organizaci\u00f3n que establece gu\u00edas y recomendaciones para el tratamiento de pacientes con enfermedad renal, incluyendo la evaluaci\u00f3n nutricional."}{"title": "HIPOALBUMINEMIA:Hipoalbuminemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of albumin in the blood. This condition can arise in various clinical contexts, including patients with inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatitis, celiac disease, and renal insufficiency. Hipoalbuminemia is often associated with poor nutritional status, which can lead to worse outcomes in surgical patients and indicate malnutrition and absorption issues in those with celiac disease. \n\nThe low levels of albumin can significantly affect drug metabolism and efficacy, as well as the measurement of calcium in the blood. Additionally, hipoalbuminemia decreases the oncotic pressure of plasma, contributing to fluid accumulation, particularly in cases of liver cirrhosis. Overall, hipoalbuminemia is a critical condition that reflects underlying health issues and can have serious implications for patient management and treatment outcomes."}{"title": "DOPPS:The Dialysis Outcomes and Practice Patterns Study (DOPPS) is a research study that evaluates the outcomes of dialysis patients and their nutritional status across various demographics in Europe and the USA."}{"title": "LEAVEY ET AL:Leavey et al is a research group that conducted a study on the relationship between body mass index and mortality in patients with renal insufficiency."}{"title": "CREATININA S\u00c9RICA:Creatinina s\u00e9rica is a serum level measurement that indicates muscle mass and protein intake in patients with terminal renal insufficiency treated with dialysis."}{"title": "DIETA HIPOPROTEICA:A hypoproteic diet is a dietary regimen that restricts protein intake, often recommended for patients with renal insufficiency."}{"title": "POLIQUISTOSIS RENAL:Polycystic kidney disease is a genetic disorder that affects kidney function and may not respond to low-protein diets."}{"title": "IRC:Chronic kidney disease (IRC) is a long-term condition where the kidneys do not work effectively, requiring dietary management."}{"title": "FALLO RENAL AGUDO:FALLO RENAL AGUDO, or acute renal failure, is characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function. This condition necessitates nutritional support and careful monitoring of electrolytes to manage the patient's health effectively."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL emphasizes the importance of nutritional support for patients with various health conditions, particularly those with renal issues. The focus is on maintaining a balanced intake of nutrients to promote overall health. Additionally, NUTRICI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL provides tailored nutritional support strategies for patients with specific health conditions, such as fibrosis qu\u00edstica, ensuring that their unique dietary needs are met effectively."}{"title": "ZARAZAGA ET AL:Zarazaga et al is a reference to a group of researchers who conducted a review on dietary recommendations for patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "KIDNEY FOUNDATION:The Kidney Foundation provides guidelines and recommendations for the nutritional management of patients with kidney disease."}{"title": "DIALYSIS PERITONEAL:DIALYSIS PERITONEAL refers to peritoneal dialysis, a treatment for kidney failure that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood. This method effectively removes toxins and excess fluids, providing an alternative to traditional hemodialysis for patients with compromised kidney function."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN LA INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR\u00d3NICA:Nutritional management in chronic kidney disease focuses on maintaining nutritional status and improving quality of life for patients."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS:Acidosis is a metabolic condition that can significantly impact patients with chronic kidney disease, influencing their nutritional status and treatment options. Additionally, it is a chronic state that affects individuals following a ketogenic diet, increasing the risk of bone demineralization. This dual impact highlights the importance of monitoring and managing acidosis in both chronic kidney disease patients and those adhering to specific dietary regimens."}{"title": "INSULINORRESISTENCIA:Insulin resistance is a condition characterized by the body's cells failing to respond effectively to insulin. This condition can complicate the management of patients with chronic kidney disease, as it impacts their nutritional needs. Additionally, insulin resistance may be exacerbated by surgical stress, further complicating the overall health and treatment of affected individuals."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS DIET\u00c9TICOS:Dietary supplements are used to ensure adequate nutrient intake in patients with chronic kidney disease, particularly those with protein restrictions."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN PREDIALISIS:Nutrition in pre-dialysis focuses on maintaining nutritional status before the initiation of dialysis treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN HEMODI\u00c1LISIS:Nutrition in hemodialysis involves specific dietary recommendations to support patients undergoing this treatment for kidney failure."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN DI\u00c1LISIS PERITONEAL:Nutrition in peritoneal dialysis addresses the unique dietary needs of patients receiving this form of kidney treatment."}{"title": "NEFROPAT\u00cdA:Nefropat\u00eda refers to kidney disease, which can be managed with dietary adjustments and nutritional support."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN PROTE\u00cdNAS:A low-protein diet is recommended for patients with renal insufficiency to manage their condition."}{"title": "RADICALES LIBRES:Free radicals are harmful compounds that can be produced in excess due to renal dysfunction, and dietary management aims to reduce their production."}{"title": "ULTRAFILTRACI\u00d3N:Ultrafiltration is a process used in dialysis to remove excess fluid from the blood."}{"title": "REAGUDIZACI\u00d3N:Reagudization refers to the worsening of a medical condition, often requiring a change in treatment or management."}{"title": "ERYTHROPOIETIN:Erythropoietin is a hormone used in the treatment of anemia, particularly in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "DIETARY ADVICE:Dietary advice is guidance provided to patients to help them meet their nutritional needs while managing dietary restrictions."}{"title": "CALORIC NEEDS:Caloric needs refer to the amount of energy required by patients, which can vary based on their medical condition, especially in renal insufficiency."}{"title": "ESTUDIO FINE:The Estudio FINE is a significant clinical study that evaluated the effects of parenteral nutrition during hemodialysis on patient outcomes over a year."}{"title": "ORTIZ ALBERTO:Ortiz Alberto is an author who contributed to the guidelines on nutrition in renal insufficiency."}{"title": "RIORO PILAR:"}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA:MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA refers to a severe form of malnutrition characterized by deficiencies in both protein and calories. This condition can arise from various factors, including the failure of renal function, which significantly impacts the overall health of the affected individual. The consequences of malnutrici\u00f3n cal\u00f3rico-proteica can be profound, leading to a deterioration in health and well-being."}{"title": "KIDNEY DISEASES OUTCOMES QUALITY INITIATIVE:The Kidney Diseases Outcomes Quality Initiative (K/DOQI) is an organization that provides guidelines for the management of kidney diseases, including nutrition guidelines for patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "DIALYSIS OUTCOMES AND PRACTICE PATTERNS STUDY:The Dialysis Outcomes and Practice Patterns Study (DOPPS) is a comprehensive research initiative that investigates various aspects of hemodialysis practices and outcomes across multiple countries. This study specifically focuses on the predictors and consequences of altered mineral metabolism in patients undergoing dialysis, as well as examining nutritional indicators and patient adherence. By analyzing these factors, DOPPS aims to enhance the understanding of dialysis outcomes and improve practice patterns in the treatment of patients with kidney failure."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF RENAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:The International Society of Renal Nutrition and Metabolism is an organization dedicated to improving the nutritional care of patients with kidney disease through research and consensus statements."}{"title": "NUTRITION GUIDELINES:The Nutrition Guidelines are a set of recommendations developed by K/DOQI and other organizations to guide healthcare providers in the nutritional management of patients with kidney disease."}{"title": "ESPEN GUIDELINES ON ENTERAL NUTRITION:The ESPEN Guidelines on Enteral Nutrition offer evidence-based recommendations aimed at the nutritional management of patients across various medical conditions. These guidelines specifically address the needs of patients with renal failure as well as those suffering from pancreatitis, ensuring a comprehensive approach to enteral nutrition tailored to different health challenges."}{"title": "ACUTE RENAL FAILURE:Acute renal failure is a medical condition characterized by a sudden decrease in kidney function, requiring nutritional management to support recovery."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASE:The American Journal of Kidney Disease is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews related to kidney disease and its management."}{"title": "CANO NJ:Cano NJ is a researcher known for his work on nutritional management in patients with kidney disease, including guidelines for enteral nutrition."}{"title": "KOPPLE JD:Kopple JD is a prominent figure in nephrology, focusing on dietary protein and energy requirements for patients with end-stage renal disease."}{"title": "HECKING E:Hecking E is a researcher involved in studies related to hemodialysis and nutritional indicators in kidney disease management."}{"title": "MCCULLOUGH KP:McCullough KP is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of nutritional practices in dialysis patients."}{"title": "FIOCCADORI E:Fiaccadori E is a researcher who has published studies on enteral nutrition in patients with acute renal failure."}{"title": "ZARAZAGA A:Zarazaga A is a researcher who has worked on nutritional support in chronic renal failure, contributing to systematic reviews in the field."}{"title": "IKIZLER TA:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VIRGEN DEL ROC\u00cdO:Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc\u00edo is a hospital in Sevilla specializing in various medical fields including Endocrinology, Nutrition, and Digestive System."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD HEP\u00c1TICA CR\u00d3NICA:\"ENFERMEDAD HEP\u00c1TICA CR\u00d3NICA\" refers to chronic liver disease (EHC), a medical condition that often presents silently and can lead to severe complications such as portal hypertension and cirrhosis. This condition encompasses a range of disorders that result in long-term liver damage, including cirrhosis and hepatitis. Chronic liver disease is associated with malabsorption, metabolic disturbances, and diabetes mellitus, which can further complicate the health of affected individuals. Additionally, it is linked to malnutrition and has an adverse impact on patient outcomes, particularly for those who are candidates for liver transplantation. Overall, chronic liver disease poses significant health risks and requires careful management to mitigate its complications."}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdAS CR\u00d3NICAS:Hepatopat\u00edas cr\u00f3nicas are chronic liver diseases that can be exacerbated by conditions of iron overload, such as hemochromatosis. These chronic liver diseases may necessitate liver transplantation as a therapeutic alternative. Additionally, hepatopat\u00edas cr\u00f3nicas can contribute to the development of iron overload conditions, highlighting the complex interplay between liver health and iron metabolism."}{"title": "VIRUS DE HEPATITIS B (VHB):Hepatitis B virus is a major cause of liver disease, affecting 1-2% of the general population and leading to cirrhosis in 30% of patients over time."}{"title": "VIRUS DE HEPATITIS C (VHC):Hepatitis C virus is another significant cause of liver disease, with a similar prevalence and progression to cirrhosis as hepatitis B."}{"title": "HEMOCRMATOSIS:Hemochromatosis is a medical condition characterized by excessive accumulation of iron in the body, which can result in significant health complications. This condition can lead to serious issues such as liver cirrhosis and diabetes mellitus, as well as liver damage. The iron overload associated with hemochromatosis poses risks to various organs, making it a critical health concern that requires careful management and treatment."}{"title": "PERITONITIS BACTERIANA ESPONT\u00c1NEA (PBE):Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis is an infection of ascitic fluid that occurs in patients with cirrhosis, often requiring medical intervention."}{"title": "CETOG\u00c9NESIS:Ketogenesis is the metabolic process by which ketone bodies are produced from fatty acids, particularly during periods of low carbohydrate intake."}{"title": "DETOXIFICACI\u00d3N DEL AMON\u00cdACO:Detoxification of ammonia is a critical liver function that converts toxic ammonia into urea for excretion, essential for maintaining metabolic balance."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTESIS DE UREA:Urea synthesis is a metabolic process that converts ammonia into urea, which is then excreted in urine, playing a vital role in nitrogen metabolism."}{"title": "METABOLISMO DEL HIERRO:Iron metabolism refers to the processes involved in the absorption, transport, and storage of iron in the body, crucial for producing hemoglobin."}{"title": "METABOLISMO DEL COBRE:Copper metabolism involves the absorption, transport, and utilization of copper, an essential trace mineral important for various enzymatic functions."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZACI\u00d3N PROLONGADA:Prolonged hospitalization refers to extended stays in a hospital, often due to complications arising from chronic conditions like liver disease."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD POSTOPERATORIA:Postoperative mortality refers to death occurring after surgical procedures, which can be influenced by factors such as malnutrition in liver transplant patients.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CHILD-PUGH CLASSIFICATION:The Child-Pugh classification is a scoring system used to assess the prognosis of chronic liver disease, particularly cirrhosis."}{"title": "MELD SCORE:The MELD score is a system used to prioritize patients for liver transplantation based on the severity of liver disease."}{"title": "VARICES GASTROESOF\u00c1GICAS:Gastroesophageal varices are dilated veins in the esophagus that can occur due to portal hypertension, often a complication of liver disease."}{"title": "HEPATOPULMONAR SYNDROME:Hepatopulmonary syndrome is a condition that affects the lungs and is associated with liver disease, leading to difficulty in oxygenation."}{"title": "MIOCARDIOPAT\u00cdA CIRR\u00d3TICA:Cirrhotic cardiomyopathy is a cardiac condition that can occur in patients with cirrhosis, affecting heart function."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME HEPATORRENAL:Hepatorenal syndrome is a serious complication of advanced liver disease characterized by kidney failure."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME HEPATODRENAL:Hepatoadrenal syndrome is a condition where adrenal function is impaired due to liver disease."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE COAGULACI\u00d3N:Coagulation disorders are common in liver disease due to impaired synthesis of clotting factors."}{"title": "LEUCO-PLAQUETOPENIA:Leukopenia and thrombocytopenia are conditions characterized by low white blood cell and platelet counts, often seen in liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN ENFERMEDAD HEP\u00c1TICA:Nutritional support is critical in managing chronic liver disease, as malnutrition is a common complication."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE DE H\u00cdGADO:The \"TRASPLANTE DE H\u00cdGADO\" is a surgical procedure that may be necessary for patients suffering from advanced liver disease. This procedure involves the replacement of a diseased liver with a healthy liver from a donor, and it is typically considered when other treatments have failed to improve the patient's condition."}{"title": "EHCA:EHCA refers to a condition associated with advanced stages of liver disease, particularly end-stage liver disease. This condition significantly impacts patients' nutritional status, leading to complications such as malnutrition and other health issues. Patients with EHCA experience metabolic alterations that pose nutritional challenges, necessitating specialized nutritional support to manage their health effectively. Overall, EHCA encompasses the various complications and health issues that arise in individuals suffering from chronic liver disease, particularly in its later stages."}{"title": "OXIDATION OF LIPIDS:The oxidation of lipids is a metabolic process that provides energy, particularly during fasting, and is heightened in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "AMMONIA:Ammonia is a compound that can accumulate in the body, particularly in liver disease, and is associated with metabolic disturbances affecting muscle function."}{"title": "NEOGLUCONEOGENESIS:Neoglucogenesis is the metabolic process of producing glucose from non-carbohydrate sources, which is altered in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "HYPERMETABOLISM:Hypermetabolism is a condition characterized by an increased metabolic rate, which is often observed in critically ill patients. This heightened metabolic state can also occur in individuals with liver disease, resulting in muscle loss and various other complications."}{"title": "CALORIMETRY:Calorimetry is a method used to measure energy expenditure, which is crucial for determining the nutritional needs of patients. This technique is particularly recommended for assessing metabolic rates in individuals with liver disease. In clinical settings, calorimetry is frequently employed to evaluate the metabolic needs of patients, providing valuable insights into their energy requirements. Overall, calorimetry serves as an important tool in understanding and managing the metabolic health of patients."}{"title": "LIPOLYSIS:"}{"title": "PACIENTE CIRR\u00d3TICO:El paciente cirr\u00f3tico es una persona que padece cirrosis, una enfermedad hep\u00e1tica cr\u00f3nica que afecta su estado nutricional y requiere valoraci\u00f3n nutricional."}{"title": "EDEMAS:EDEMAS refers to swellings that occur due to excess fluid being trapped in the body's tissues. This condition can be particularly concerning for patients with kidney issues, as it may indicate underlying health problems. Additionally, edemas can complicate nutritional assessments in patients with cirrhosis, as the accumulation of fluid in the tissues can affect overall health and nutritional status."}{"title": "RESTRICCIONES DIET\u00c9TICAS:Las restricciones diet\u00e9ticas son limitaciones en la ingesta de ciertos alimentos que pueden ser necesarias para el manejo del paciente cirr\u00f3tico."}{"title": "MUSCLE STRENGTH:Muscle strength is a vital component in evaluating the nutritional status of patients with cirrhosis and plays a significant role in the assessment of sarcopenia. It is commonly measured using handgrip dynamometry, which is a standard method for quantifying muscle strength. Additionally, muscle strength can be assessed through various tests, including handgrip strength and knee extension. Overall, muscle strength serves as an important physical attribute that reflects an individual's health and functional capacity."}{"title": "BIOELECTRICAL IMPEDANCE ANALYSIS:Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a method used to estimate body composition, including fat and lean mass, which is relevant in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL NUTRITIONAL PRIORITIZING TOOL:The Royal Free Hospital Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) is a global scheme for assessing nutritional risk in patients with cirrhosis."}{"title": "PACIENTES CIRR\u00d3TICOS:PACIENTES CIRR\u00d3TICOS refers to individuals suffering from cirrhosis, a serious liver condition that often leads to nutritional deficiencies. These patients require specific dietary assessments and nutritional guidelines to effectively manage their condition. Proper nutrition is crucial for cirrhotic patients to support their health and mitigate the complications associated with their illness."}{"title": "ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL:The Royal Free Hospital is a healthcare institution that utilizes the Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) for assessing malnutrition risks in patients."}{"title": "EHC:EHC refers to patients with chronic liver disease, particularly those experiencing sarcopenia, which is a significant concern in nutritional management."}{"title": "RESTRICCI\u00d3N DE SODIO:Sodium restriction is a dietary intervention often recommended for patients with liver conditions to manage fluid retention and ascites."}{"title": "RESTRICCI\u00d3N DE PROTE\u00cdNAS:Protein restriction is a dietary practice that is generally discouraged in patients with liver disease, as it can worsen nutritional status."}{"title": "AUMENTO DE MASA GRASA:Increase in fat mass can occur in patients with liver disease if caloric intake is not properly managed."}{"title": "ECHA:ECHA refers to a condition related to hepatic encephalopathy and nutritional deficiencies in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "FOLIC ACID:Folic acid is a water-soluble B vitamin that plays a vital role in DNA synthesis and repair, making it particularly important during pregnancy. It is essential for the proper development of the fetus and helps prevent neural tube defects. Additionally, folic acid is often found to be deficient in individuals with alcohol-related liver disease, highlighting its significance in overall health and nutrition."}{"title": "SANGRADO:SANGRADO refers to bleeding, which can manifest as a complication in various medical contexts. In patients with liver disease, bleeding may lead to episodes of hepatic encephalopathy, a serious condition affecting brain function. Additionally, bleeding is a potential complication associated with the use of central venous access for nutritional support, indicating the risks involved in such medical procedures. Furthermore, in patients with gastrointestinal bleeding (GEP), bleeding is considered a minor complication that may arise due to damage to the vasculature at the site of implantation. Overall, SANGRADO encompasses various scenarios where bleeding can pose significant health risks, particularly in patients with underlying conditions."}{"title": "ABUSO DE SUSTANCIAS:Substance abuse can lead to liver damage and is a significant factor in the development of hepatic encephalopathy."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ORIGEN ALCOH\u00d3LICO:Alcoholic liver disease is a condition caused by excessive alcohol consumption, leading to liver damage and complications."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ENRIQUECIDAS EN AACR:Enriched formulas in AACR are specialized nutritional formulas designed to provide additional nutrients for patients, particularly those with liver disease."}{"title": "COLANGITIS:Cholangitis is an infection of the bile duct that can complicate liver disease and affect nutritional status."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD EUROPEA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL:ESPEN is an organization that provides guidelines for enteral nutrition, recommending early nutritional support for patients post-liver transplant."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE RENUTRICI\u00d3N:Refeeding syndrome is a dangerous condition that can occur when feeding is restarted in malnourished patients, leading to severe electrolyte imbalances."}{"title": "EJERCICIO AER\u00d3BICO Y DE RESISTENCIA:Aerobic and resistance exercise are recommended for improving physical activity levels in patients recovering from liver transplant."}{"title": "TIPS:TIPS, or Transjugular Intrahepatic Portosystemic Shunt, is a medical procedure designed to address portal hypertension, which is frequently associated with liver disease. This procedure is particularly beneficial for treating conditions such as quilot\u00f3rax that arise as a secondary complication of portal hypertension. By creating a shunt, TIPS offers a potential resolution for these conditions, improving patient outcomes related to elevated portal pressure."}{"title": "CIRRHOSIS HEPATICA:Cirrhosis is a severe liver condition that can lead to malnutrition and other complications in patients."}{"title": "KALAFATELI M:Kalafateli M is an author of a study that discusses the impact of malnutrition and sarcopenia on post-liver transplantation outcomes."}{"title": "MANTZOUKIS K:Mantzoukis K is a co-author of research related to malnutrition and sarcopenia in liver disease patients."}{"title": "CHOI YAU Y:Choi Yau Y is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition and sarcopenia in liver transplantation outcomes."}{"title": "SPANISH LIVER TRANSPLANT REGISTRY:The Spanish Liver Transplant Registry collects data on liver transplant outcomes and is referenced in the context of liver disease management."}{"title": "SUPPLEMENTS:Supplements are additional nutritional products that are recommended for patients who cannot meet their dietary needs through food alone."}{"title": "POST-LIVER TRANSPLANTATION:Post-liver transplantation refers to the period after a liver transplant, where patients require careful nutritional management."}{"title": "MUSCLE DEPLETION:Muscle depletion is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, which poses significant health risks. It is particularly concerning in patients with liver cirrhosis, as it increases the risk of hepatic encephalopathy, a serious complication of liver dysfunction. Additionally, muscle depletion is a critical issue in cancer patients, where it is often linked to cancer cachexia\u2014a syndrome that leads to severe weight loss and muscle wasting. This condition adversely affects the prognosis of cancer patients, highlighting the importance of addressing muscle depletion in both liver disease and cancer care."}{"title": "HEPATIC ENCEPHALOPATHY:Hepatic encephalopathy is a decline in brain function that occurs as a result of severe liver disease. This condition leads to a buildup of toxins in the bloodstream, which can significantly impair cognitive function and overall neurological health."}{"title": "CIRRHOSIS:Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by the replacement of healthy liver tissue with scar tissue, which leads to liver dysfunction and can progress to liver failure. It represents a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver, resulting from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis and chronic alcoholism. Additionally, cirrhosis increases the risk of developing hepatocellular carcinoma, a type of liver cancer."}{"title": "MELD:MELD (Model for End-Stage Liver Disease) is a scoring system used to assess the severity of chronic liver disease and prioritize patients for liver transplantation."}{"title": "PROTEIN-CALORIE MALNUTRITION:Protein-calorie malnutrition is a condition that occurs when the body does not get enough protein and calories, which can be particularly detrimental in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "MONTANO-LOZA AJ:Montano-Loza AJ is a researcher and author known for his significant contributions to the field of liver transplantation and cirrhosis. He has published studies focusing on muscle wasting and its implications for liver transplantation outcomes. Additionally, Montano-Loza AJ has investigated the association between sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass, and mortality in patients suffering from cirrhosis. His work highlights the critical relationship between muscle health and patient prognosis in liver-related diseases."}{"title": "TANDON P:Tandon P is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of liver health. They have studied the prevalence of severe muscle depletion in patients on the liver transplant waitlist, highlighting the critical health challenges faced by these individuals. Additionally, Tandon P has contributed to a meta-analysis on nutritional supplementation in cirrhosis, further emphasizing their commitment to advancing knowledge and improving patient outcomes in liver disease."}{"title": "HARA N:Hara N is a researcher who has investigated the prognostic factors for overall survival in patients with cirrhosis."}{"title": "CARIAS S:Carias S is a researcher who has studied the association between nonalcoholic steatohepatitis and sarcopenic obesity in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "PERIYALWAR P:Periyalwar P is a researcher who has explored the consequences of malnutrition in cirrhosis."}{"title": "MCULLOUGH AJ:McCullough AJ is a researcher who has studied protein-calorie malnutrition and its role in the etiology of cirrhosis."}{"title": "LAUTZ H U:Lautz H U is a researcher who has investigated protein-calorie malnutrition in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "DASARATHY S:"}{"title": "LIVER INT:Liver Int, also known as Liver International, is a medical journal dedicated to publishing research on liver diseases and related topics. The journal focuses on a wide range of subjects, including studies on cirrhosis and the nutritional aspects of liver health. It serves as a platform for disseminating important findings and advancements in the field of hepatology."}{"title": "JPEN:JPEN, or the Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition, is a specialized publication dedicated to the field of nutrition support, particularly focusing on parenteral and enteral nutrition. The journal publishes clinical guidelines, research findings, and studies related to nutritional therapy and management, addressing various nutritional parameters in patients. It serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals, providing insights into nutrition science, especially in clinical settings such as liver disease. Through its comprehensive coverage of research and guidelines, JPEN aims to advance the understanding and application of nutrition support in medical practice."}{"title": "MAYO CLIN PROC:Mayo Clinic Proceedings is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews in clinical medicine. It covers a wide range of medical topics, including but not limited to liver transplantation. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings and advancements in the field of medicine, contributing to the ongoing education and knowledge of healthcare professionals."}{"title": "HEPATOLOGY:Hepatology is both a specialized branch of medicine and a journal dedicated to the study, diagnosis, and treatment of liver diseases. This field encompasses a wide range of liver-related conditions, including cirrhosis and its complications. The journal serves as a platform for publishing research that advances the understanding and management of these diseases, contributing significantly to the medical community's knowledge in hepatology."}{"title": "MCCLAINS:McClain CJ is a researcher known for work on nutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "FIGUEIREDO FA:Figueiredo FA is a researcher and author who specializes in the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to liver health. He is involved in comparing various nutritional assessment methods specifically for patients with liver cirrhosis. Additionally, Figueiredo FA has conducted studies focusing on nutritional parameters in patients suffering from end-stage liver disease, contributing valuable insights to the understanding of nutrition's role in liver conditions."}{"title": "DICECCO SR:DiCecco SR is a researcher who assessed nutritional status in patients undergoing liver transplantation."}{"title": "ALBERINO F:Alberino F is a researcher who studied nutrition and survival in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "FERREIRA LG:Ferreira LG is a researcher who examined negative energy balance in patients on the liver transplant waiting list."}{"title": "MADDEN AM:Madden AM is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the study of cirrhosis. They have conducted research on taste perception in patients with cirrhosis, exploring how this condition affects sensory experiences. Additionally, Madden AM has authored a comparative study on skinfold anthropometry and bioelectrical impedance analysis in cirrhosis, highlighting the importance of these methods in assessing body composition in affected individuals. Through their work, Madden AM has provided valuable insights into the complexities of cirrhosis and its impact on various physiological aspects."}{"title": "DAVIDSON HIM:Davidson HIM is a researcher who investigated dietary intake among stable cirrhotic patients."}{"title": "AQEL BA:Aqel BA is a researcher who studied the impact of ascites on gastric function in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "RICHARDSON RA:Richardson RA is a researcher who explored the metabolic effects of liver cirrhosis on nutritional intake."}{"title": "ZOCCO E:Zocco E is a researcher who studied the role of cytokines in protein metabolism in liver disease."}{"title": "MCCULLOUGH AJ:McCullough AJ is a researcher who examined gender-dependent alterations in serum leptin in alcoholic cirrhosis."}{"title": "NICOLAS JM:Nicol\u00e1s JM is a researcher who studied circulating leptin levels in chronic alcoholism."}{"title": "TESTA R:Testa R is a researcher who investigated serum leptin levels in patients with viral chronic hepatitis or liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "GRECO AV:Greco AV is a researcher who studied serum leptin levels in post-hepatitis liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "ONODERA K:Onodera K is a researcher who examined serum leptin concentrations in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "OCKENGA J:Ockenga J is a researcher and author known for his contributions to the field of medical research, particularly in relation to nutrition and metabolic disorders. He studied the correlation of bound leptin with energy expenditure in patients suffering from cirrhosis, providing insights into the metabolic changes associated with this condition. Additionally, Ockenga J researched the effects of glutamine-enriched total parenteral nutrition in patients with acute pancreatitis, highlighting the importance of nutritional support in managing this serious condition. Furthermore, he reviewed the topics of anorexia and cachexia in gastrointestinal cancer, contributing to the understanding of these complex issues that affect patients with cancer. Through his work, Ockenga J has made significant contributions to the understanding of nutrition and metabolism in various clinical contexts."}{"title": "ROMITI A:Romiti A is a researcher who investigated malabsorption and nutritional abnormalities in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "MUELLER MJ:Muller MJ is a researcher who examined glucose intolerance in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "BIANCHI G:Bianchi G is a researcher who studied the prognostic significance of diabetes in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "IMANO E:Imano E is a researcher who investigated impaired glucose uptake in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "CHANGANI KK:Changani KK is a researcher who provided evidence for altered hepatic gluconeogenesis in cirrhosis."}{"title": "MARSANO L:"}{"title": "LIVER CIRRHOSIS:Liver cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease marked by the progressive replacement of healthy liver tissue with scar tissue, which significantly impairs liver function and metabolism. It represents a late stage of scarring, known as fibrosis, resulting from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis and chronic alcoholism."}{"title": "JOHN DOE:John Doe is a hypothetical patient used in clinical studies to represent individuals with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "ENERGY EXPENDITURE:Energy expenditure refers to the total amount of energy used by the body. This measurement can be influenced by various factors, including metabolic changes that occur in patients with liver cirrhosis. In such individuals, the body's energy expenditure may be altered, reflecting the impact of the disease on metabolic processes."}{"title": "PROTEIN DEPLETION:Protein depletion is a condition that can occur in patients with liver cirrhosis, affecting their nutritional status and overall health."}{"title": "BODY COMPOSITION ANALYSIS:Body composition analysis is a method used to assess the nutritional status of patients with liver cirrhosis, helping to identify protein depletion."}{"title": "MULTIVARIATE ANALYSIS:Multivariate analysis is a statistical method used to understand the relationship between multiple variables, such as nutritional factors and survival in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "ASCITES:Ascites is the accumulation of fluid in the abdominal cavity, commonly associated with cirrhosis and liver disease. It is often observed in patients suffering from liver cirrhosis, which can impact their energy expenditure. Additionally, ascites can be related to various medical conditions, including chylous ascites, highlighting its multifaceted nature in clinical presentations."}{"title": "ALCOHOLIC CIRRHOSIS:"}{"title": "CAMPILLO B:Campillo B is an author engaged in research focused on body mass index and malnutrition. Additionally, Campillo B has contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on parenteral nutrition in the field of hepatology. This involvement highlights Campillo B's expertise and commitment to advancing knowledge in nutrition and its implications for health."}{"title": "PILLAUD E:Pillaud E is a co-author contributing to the study on body mass index and malnutrition."}{"title": "UZAN I:Uzan I is a co-author of the research paper discussing the value of body mass index in detecting severe malnutrition."}{"title": "HUMAN BODY COMPOSITION:Human Body Composition is a book edited by Ellis K J and Eastman J D, discussing various aspects of body composition."}{"title": "LIVER TRANSPLANT:Liver transplant refers to a surgical procedure in which a diseased liver is replaced with a healthy liver from a donor. This procedure often requires careful nutritional assessment both before and after the operation to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Additionally, the topic of liver transplantation is explored in the journal \"Liver Transpl,\" which publishes studies related to nutritional parameters in liver disease, highlighting the importance of nutrition in the management and treatment of liver conditions."}{"title": "KOREAN JOURNAL OF INTERNAL MEDICINE:Korean J Intern Med is a journal that published a study on body composition assessment in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "JEBB SA:Jebb SA is a co-author involved in research focused on body composition measurement. Additionally, Jebb SA has conducted a pilot study examining the effects of oral glutamine supplementation in patients undergoing bone marrow transplants."}{"title": "GOLDBERG GR:Goldberg GR is a co-author contributing to the study on body composition measurement."}{"title": "BRAMLEY P:Bramley P is an author who researched body composition analysis in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "OLDROYD B:Oldroyd B is a co-author of the study on body composition analysis in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "STEWART S:Stewart S is a co-author involved in the research on body composition in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "FIORE P:Fiore P is an author who compared skinfold anthropometry and dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry in cirrhotic patients."}{"title": "MERLI M:Merli M is a co-author of a study that compares body fat evaluation methods in cirrhotic patients. Additionally, Merli M has conducted research on the risk of health care-associated bacterial infections in this same patient population. Through these contributions, Merli M has focused on important health issues affecting individuals with cirrhosis."}{"title": "ANDREOLI A:Andreoli A is a co-author involved in the research on body fat evaluation in cirrhotic patients."}{"title": "DICKSON ER:Dickson ER is a co-author contributing to the study on nutritional parameters in liver disease."}{"title": "PASHA TM:Pasha TM is a co-author involved in the research on body cell mass depletion in liver disease."}{"title": "DETSKY AS:Detsky AS is an author who discussed subjective global assessment of nutritional status."}{"title": "MCLAUGHLIN JR:McLaughlin JR is a co-author of the study on subjective global assessment."}{"title": "BAKER JP:Baker JP is a co-author involved in the research on subjective global assessment."}{"title": "JOHNSTON N:Johnston N is a co-author contributing to the study on subjective global assessment."}{"title": "WHITTAKER J:Whittaker J is a co-author involved in the research on subjective global assessment."}{"title": "MENDELSON RA:Mendelson RA is a co-author of the study on subjective global assessment."}{"title": "HASSE J:Hasse J is an author who discussed alternative nutrition-assessment techniques for liver-transplant candidates."}{"title": "STRONG S:Strong S is a co-author involved in the research on nutrition-assessment techniques."}{"title": "GORMAN MA:Gorman MA is a co-author contributing to the study on nutrition-assessment techniques."}{"title": "ALVAREZ-DA-SILVA MR:Alvares-da-Silva MR is an author who compared various nutritional assessment methods in cirrhotic patients."}{"title": "REVERBEL DA SILVEIRA T:Reverbel da Silveira T is a co-author involved in the study on nutritional assessment methods."}{"title": "BALLMER PE:Ballmer PE is an author who studied albumin synthesis rates in cirrhosis."}{"title": "WALSHE D:Walshe D is a co-author contributing to the research on albumin synthesis in cirrhosis."}{"title": "MCNURLAN MA:McNurlan MA is a co-author involved in the study on albumin synthesis rates."}{"title": "WATSON H:Watson H is a co-author contributing to the research on albumin synthesis in cirrhosis."}{"title": "BRUNT PW:Brunt PW is a co-author involved in the study on albumin synthesis rates in cirrhosis."}{"title": "GARLICK PJ:Garlick PJ is a co-author contributing to the research on albumin synthesis in cirrhosis."}{"title": "ARANDA-MICHEL J:Aranda-Michel J is an author discussing nutrition in hepatic failure and liver transplantation."}{"title": "CRAWFORD DHG:Crawford DHG is an author who studied malnutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "CUNEO RC:Cuneo RC is a co-author involved in the research on malnutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "SHEPHERD RW:Shepherd RW is a co-author contributing to the study on malnutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "SELBERG O:Selberg O is a co-author involved in the research on estimating skeletal muscle mass."}{"title": "BOKER K:Boker K is a co-author contributing to the study on estimating skeletal muscle mass in cirrhosis."}{"title": "FRANCOZ C:Francoz C is an author who has contributed to the field of medical research, particularly focusing on muscle atrophy in cirrhosis. Additionally, Francoz C has studied the inaccuracies associated with creatinine-based equations in candidates for liver transplantation. Through these studies, Francoz C has provided valuable insights into the challenges faced in managing liver-related health issues."}{"title": "PRIE D:Prie D is a co-author involved in the research on creatinine-based equations."}{"title": "ABDELRAZEK W:Abdelrazek W is a co-author contributing to the study on creatinine inaccuracies."}{"title": "SCHLOERB PR:Schloerb PR is an author who studied bioelectrical impedance in liver disease evaluation."}{"title": "FORSTER J:Forster J is a co-author involved in the research on bioelectrical impedance."}{"title": "DELCOR R:Delcore R is a co-author contributing to the study on bioelectrical impedance in liver disease."}{"title": "MORGAN MY:Morgan MY is a co-author involved in the research on body fat measurement in cirrhosis."}{"title": "CABRE E:Cabre E is an author who has made significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to liver disease. He is involved in the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition specifically tailored for patients with liver conditions. Additionally, Cabre E has conducted research focusing on the nutritional aspects of chronic liver disease, enhancing the understanding of dietary needs in this patient population. Furthermore, he has studied the reliability of bioelectrical impedance analysis as a method for assessing body composition in individuals with cirrhosis, contributing valuable insights into the management of this condition."}{"title": "DE LEON R:De Leon R is a co-author contributing to the study on bioelectrical impedance in cirrhosis."}{"title": "PLANAS R:Planas R is a co-author involved in the research on bioelectrical impedance analysis."}{"title": "FERNANDES SA:Fernandes SA is an author recognized for their contributions to research on nutritional assessment in patients with cirrhosis. Their work focuses on the evaluation of nutritional status and its implications for individuals suffering from this liver condition, highlighting the importance of proper nutritional management in the treatment of cirrhosis."}{"title": "BASSANI L:Bassani L is a co-author and contributor to research focused on nutritional assessment in patients with cirrhosis. They have collaborated on various studies that explore the nutritional needs and evaluations specific to this patient population, highlighting the importance of proper nutritional management in the context of cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUNES FF:Nunes FF is a co-author and contributor to research focused on nutritional assessment and evaluation in individuals with cirrhosis. This involvement highlights Nunes FF's engagement in studies aimed at understanding the nutritional needs and challenges faced by patients suffering from this liver condition."}{"title": "AYDOS ME:Aydos ME is a co-author and contributor to research focused on nutritional assessment in patients with cirrhosis. Through their work, Aydos ME has played a significant role in advancing the understanding of nutritional needs and interventions for individuals suffering from this liver condition."}{"title": "ALVES AV:Alves AV is a co-author and an author involved in research focused on nutritional assessment in cirrhosis. This work contributes to the understanding of nutritional needs and management in patients suffering from this liver condition."}{"title": "MARRONI CA:Marroni CA is a co-author and an author who has contributed to the research on nutritional assessment in patients with cirrhosis. This work focuses on evaluating the nutritional status and needs of individuals suffering from this liver condition, highlighting the importance of proper nutrition in managing cirrhosis."}{"title": "SCHUTZ T:Schutz T is an author recognized for contributions to the field of gastroenterology, particularly in the areas of malnutrition assessment in cirrhosis and enteral nutrition. He has participated in studies that focus on evaluating malnutrition in patients with liver disease and has also co-authored discussions on the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) guidelines regarding enteral nutrition practices. Through his work, Schutz T has played a significant role in advancing the understanding and management of nutritional issues in gastroenterological conditions."}{"title": "SPACHOS T:Spachos T is an author involved in research on bioelectrical impedance analysis in cirrhosis."}{"title": "LLAMES L:Llames L is an author who studied the phase angle by bioelectrical impedance in relation to nutritional status."}{"title": "BALDOMERO V:Baldomero V is an author who contributed to research on nutritional status in cirrhosis."}{"title": "IGLESIAS ML:Iglesias ML is an author involved in studies on nutritional assessment in cirrhosis."}{"title": "RODOTA LP:Rodota LP is an author who has researched nutritional status in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "DURAND F:Durand F is an author who studied the prognostic value of muscle atrophy in cirrhosis."}{"title": "BUYSE S:Buyse S is an author who contributed to research on muscle atrophy in cirrhosis."}{"title": "LAOUENAN C:Laouenan C is an author who studied muscle atrophy in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "BRUNO O:Bruno O is an author who contributed to research on muscle atrophy in cirrhosis."}{"title": "BELGHITI J:Belghiti J is an author involved in studies on muscle atrophy in cirrhosis."}{"title": "GIUSTO M:Giusto M is an author who studied sarcopenia in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "LATTANZI B:Lattanzi B is an author engaged in research focused on muscle mass assessment in patients with cirrhosis. This research includes a specific emphasis on sarcopenia, which is the loss of muscle mass and strength, and its effects on individuals suffering from liver cirrhosis. Through this work, Lattanzi B contributes to a deeper understanding of the implications of muscle deterioration in this patient population."}{"title": "ALBANESE C:Albanese C is an author who contributed to studies on muscle mass in cirrhosis."}{"title": "GALTIERI A:Galtieri A is an author involved in research on muscle mass in cirrhosis."}{"title": "FARCOMENI A:Farcomeni A is an author who studied muscle mass in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "GIANNELLI V:Giannelli V is an author engaged in research focused on muscle mass in cirrhosis, particularly examining the condition of sarcopenia and its implications for the prognosis of liver cirrhosis. Through their contributions, Giannelli V has highlighted the significance of muscle mass in understanding and managing the outcomes of patients suffering from liver-related diseases."}{"title": "WANG CW:Wang CW is an author who studied muscle function and mass in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "FENG S:Feng S is an author involved in research on muscle function in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "COVINSKY KE:Covinsky KE is an author who contributed to studies on muscle function in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "HAYSSEN H:Hayssen H is an author involved in research on muscle function in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "ZHOU LQ:Zhou LQ is an author who studied muscle function in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "YEH BM:Yeh BM is an author involved in research on muscle function in liver transplant candidates."}{"title": "RIGGIO O:Riggio O is an author who contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "ASSIS-CAMILO M:Assis-Camilo M is an author involved in the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in liver disease."}{"title": "BORHOFEN SM:Borhofen SM is an author who studied the Royal Free Hospital-Nutritional Prioritizing Tool in cirrhosis."}{"title": "GERNER C:Gerner C is an author involved in research on nutritional prioritizing in cirrhosis."}{"title": "LEHMANN J:Lehmann J is an author who contributed to studies on nutritional prioritizing in cirrhosis."}{"title": "NANGLIYA V:Nangliya V is an author who studied trace elements in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "SHARMA A:Sharma A is an author involved in research on trace elements in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "YADAV D:Yadav D is an author who contributed to studies on trace elements in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "GUERRA TS:Guerra TS is an author who studied trace elements in plasma of cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "HOEHR NF:Hoehr NF is an author involved in research on nutritional assessment in cirrhosis."}{"title": "BOIN IDE F:Boin Ide F is an author who studied nutritional assessment in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "STUCCHI RS:Stucchi RS is an author involved in research on nutritional assessment in cirrhosis."}{"title": "KOLACHI NF:Kolachi NF is an author who studied essential trace and toxic elements in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "KAZI TG:Kazi TG is an author involved in research on trace elements in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "AFRIDI HI:Afridi HI is an author who studied trace elements in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "KAZI NG:Kazi NG is an author involved in research on trace elements in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "KHAN S:Khan S is an author who studied trace elements in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "GASSULL MA:Gassull MA is an author engaged in research focusing on the nutritional aspects of chronic liver disease. Additionally, Gassull MA has reviewed the role of nutrition in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease, highlighting the importance of dietary considerations in managing these health conditions."}{"title": "PHILLIPS JR:Phillips JR is an author who studied fat-soluble vitamin levels in primary biliary cirrhosis."}{"title": "ANGULO P:Angulo P is an author involved in research(\"entity\""}{"title": "TRACE ELEMENTS:TRACE ELEMENTS are essential nutrients that play a critical role in various bodily functions, including recovery from burn injuries. These minerals are present in small amounts in the body and are vital for numerous physiological processes. Additionally, the levels of trace elements can be affected by conditions such as liver cirrhosis, highlighting their importance in maintaining overall health and supporting recovery in different medical contexts."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL PRIORITIZING TOOL:The Royal Free Hospital-Nutritional Prioritizing Tool is a method used to assess nutritional needs in patients, particularly those with liver disease."}{"title": "FUNCTIONAL ASSESSMENT IN LIVER TRANSPLANTATION STUDY:This study evaluates muscle function, mass, and quality in candidates for liver transplantation, providing insights into their nutritional status."}{"title": "DUAL-ENERGY X-RAY ABSORPTIOMETRY:Dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry is a technique used to measure bone density and body composition, including muscle mass in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY:Computed tomography is an imaging technique used to assess muscle mass and other anatomical features in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "ALCOHOLIC HEPATITIS:Alcoholic hepatitis is a liver condition caused by excessive alcohol consumption, often leading to malnutrition and cirrhosis."}{"title": "PRIMARY BILIARY CIRRHOSIS:Primary biliary cirrhosis is a chronic disease that slowly destroys the bile ducts in the liver, leading to cirrhosis and nutritional issues."}{"title": "MUSCLE ATROPHY:Muscle atrophy is the loss of muscle mass that can occur in patients with cirrhosis. This condition is often associated with poor nutritional status, highlighting the importance of adequate nutrition in maintaining muscle health."}{"title": "PHASE ANGLE:Phase angle is a measure derived from bioelectrical impedance analysis that can indicate nutritional status and cellular health in patients with cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL ASPECTS OF CHRONIC LIVER DISEASE:This refers to the various dietary and nutritional considerations that are important for managing chronic liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL EVALUATION IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional evaluation in cirrhosis focuses on assessing the dietary needs and nutritional status of patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "MALNUTRITION IN CIRRHOSIS:Malnutrition in cirrhosis refers to the inadequate intake or absorption of nutrients in patients suffering from liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT TOOLS:Nutritional assessment tools are instruments used to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES FOR LIVER DISEASE:Nutritional guidelines for liver disease provide specific dietary recommendations to manage liver conditions effectively."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STATUS ASSESSMENT:Nutritional status assessment involves evaluating the dietary intake and nutritional health of patients, especially those with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional support in cirrhosis refers to dietary interventions aimed at improving the health of patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTIONS IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional interventions in cirrhosis are strategies implemented to enhance the nutritional status of patients with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STRATEGIES FOR CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional strategies for cirrhosis involve dietary approaches tailored to improve the health of patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL OUTCOMES IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional outcomes in cirrhosis refer to the results of dietary interventions and assessments in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional assessment in cirrhosis focuses on evaluating the dietary needs and nutritional status of patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES FOR CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional guidelines for cirrhosis provide dietary recommendations to manage the condition effectively."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL THERAPY IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional therapy in cirrhosis involves dietary practices aimed at improving the health of patients with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STRATEGIES IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional strategies in cirrhosis are dietary approaches designed to enhance the nutritional status of patients with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL RESEARCH IN CIRRHOSIS:Nutritional research in cirrhosis focuses on studying dietary practices and their effects on patients with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL OUTCOMES IN LIVER DISEASE:Nutritional outcomes in liver disease"}{"title": "JOURNAL OF HEPATOLOGY:The Journal of Hepatology is a prominent peer-reviewed medical journal that specializes in the field of liver disease. It is recognized for publishing a wide range of research articles and reviews that cover various aspects of hepatology. The journal focuses on liver diseases and related topics, including clinical guidelines and specific conditions such as Wilson's disease. As a leading publication in its field, the Journal of Hepatology plays a crucial role in disseminating important findings and advancements in liver health and disease management."}{"title": "TRANSPLANTATION:Transplantation is a journal that publishes articles related to organ transplantation, including liver transplants."}{"title": "BENDTSEN F:Bendtsen F is an author who co-authored a study on prognostic variables in patients with cirrhosis and oesophageal varices."}{"title": "CHRISTENSEN E:Christensen E is an author involved in research regarding patients with cirrhosis and oesophageal varices."}{"title": "HEURIKSEN J H:Heuriksen J H is an author who contributed to the study of prognostic variables in patients with cirrhosis and oesophageal varices."}{"title": "TAJIKA M:Tajika M is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the study of liver cirrhosis. Their work focuses on nutritional interventions and energy metabolism in patients suffering from this condition. Through their research, Tajika M has aimed to enhance the understanding of how dietary and metabolic factors can impact the health and treatment of individuals with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "KATO M:Kato M is a researcher and author who has focused on the effects of extra-carbohydrate supplementation in patients with liver cirrhosis. In addition to this research, Kato M co-authored a study that examined energy metabolism in the context of liver cirrhosis, contributing valuable insights to the understanding of this condition."}{"title": "MIWA Y:Miwa Y is an author known for her contributions to research on energy metabolism in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "MOHRI H:Mohri H is a researcher and author who focuses on the study of energy supplementation and energy metabolism in patients with liver cirrhosis. Their work involves investigating how energy intake affects individuals suffering from this condition, contributing valuable insights to the understanding of nutritional needs and metabolic processes in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "MORIWAKI H:Moriwaki H is an author who contributed to research on energy metabolism in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "KALAITZAKIS E:Kalaitzakis E is an author who studied the relationship between malnutrition, diabetes, and hepatic encephalopathy in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "OLSSON R:Olsson R is an author who co-authored a study on malnutrition and diabetes in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "HENFRIDSSON P:Henfridsson P is an author involved in research on malnutrition and hepatic encephalopathy in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "LUCIDI C:Lucidi C is an author who studied the relationship between sarcopenia and prognosis in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "NARDELLI S:Nardelli S is an author who studied the impact of sarcopenia on hepatic encephalopathy development."}{"title": "TORRISI S:Torrisi S is an author who studied the relationship between sarcopenia and hepatic encephalopathy."}{"title": "ENGLESBE MJ:Englesbe MJ is an author who researched the impact of sarcopenia on mortality after liver transplantation."}{"title": "PATEL SP:Patel SP is an author who studied the relationship between sarcopenia and liver transplantation outcomes."}{"title": "MEZA-JUNCO J:Meza-Junco J is an author who contributed to research on sarcopenia and liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "PRADO CM:Prado CM is an author who studied the impact of nutritional status on liver transplantation outcomes."}{"title": "IRITANI S:Iritani S is an author who researched skeletal muscle depletion as a prognostic factor for hepatocellular carcinoma."}{"title": "IMAI K:Imai K is an author involved in research on skeletal muscle depletion and liver cancer."}{"title": "TAKAI K:Takai K is an author who studied the impact of skeletal muscle depletion on liver cancer prognosis."}{"title": "NEY M:Ney M is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on nutritional supplementation in cirrhosis."}{"title": "VANDERMEER B:Vandermeer B is an author who co-authored a meta-analysis on nutritional supplementation in liver disease."}{"title": "VAN ZANTEN SJ:Van Zanten SJ is an author involved in research on nutritional supplementation in cirrhosis."}{"title": "GRAMLICH L:Gramlich L is an author recognized for contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in surgical contexts. They played a significant role in the consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, highlighting their expertise in nutritional practices related to surgery. Additionally, Gramlich L has conducted research on the effects of nutritional supplementation in liver disease, further demonstrating their commitment to advancing knowledge in nutritional health and its implications for various medical conditions."}{"title": "CABR\u00c9 E:Cabr\u00e9 E is an author involved in the ESPEN guidelines on nutritional support for liver disease."}{"title": "MARCHESINI G:Marchesini G is an author who contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on nutritional support in hepatology."}{"title": "SCH\u00dcTZ T:Sch\u00fctz T is an author involved in the ESPEN guidelines on nutritional support for liver disease."}{"title": "SHENKIN A:Shenkin A is an author who contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on parenteral nutrition in hepatology."}{"title": "WENDON J:Wendon J is an author involved in the ESPEN guidelines on nutritional support for liver disease."}{"title": "M\u00d8LLER S:"}{"title": "DIETARY SODIUM RESTRICTION:Dietary sodium restriction is a dietary approach often recommended for patients with liver cirrhosis to manage fluid retention and other complications."}{"title": "BRANCHED CHAIN AMINO ACIDS:Branched chain amino acids (BCAAs) are essential nutrients that the body obtains from proteins found in food, often used in supplementation for patients with liver disease."}{"title": "MJA:The Medical Journal of Australia (MJA) is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews on various health topics, including liver diseases."}{"title": "NUTR CLIN PRACT:\"NUTR CLIN PRACT\" is a journal dedicated to the field of clinical nutrition and its significant implications for patient care. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including the management of chyle leaks and the nutritional needs of burn patients. The journal serves as a platform for guidelines and research related to clinical nutrition practices, emphasizing the role of nutrition in various clinical settings, including studies pertinent to liver health. Notably, it is also the publication venue for Krenitsky's work on adjusted body weight, further highlighting its commitment to advancing knowledge in clinical nutrition. Overall, \"NUTR CLIN PRACT\" plays a crucial role in disseminating research and best practices in the field of clinical nutrition."}{"title": "SHIRAKI M:Shiraki M is a researcher involved in the study of fuel metabolism in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "MURAKAMI N:Murakami N is a researcher who studied the effects of dietary interventions in liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "SWART GR:Swart GR is a researcher who studied the effects of late evening meals on patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "AOYAMA K:Aoyama K is a researcher who studied the effects of late evening snacks on outpatients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "TSIEN CD:Tsien CD is a researcher who explored the metabolic responses to late evening snacks in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "GU XB:Gu XB is a researcher who studied the effects of dietary sodium on ascites in liver cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "ZHU YF:Zhu YF is a researcher who investigated the influence of sodium-restricted diets on patients with cirrhotic ascites."}{"title": "SOULSBY CT:Soulsby CT is a researcher who studied the effects of dietary sodium restriction on energy and protein intake in cirrhosis patients."}{"title": "SEYMOUR CA:Seymour CA is a researcher who discussed dietary management of hepatic encephalopathy."}{"title": "LIVER DISEASE:Liver disease encompasses a variety of conditions that impact the liver's function and structure, including serious ailments such as cirrhosis and liver cancer. It can also manifest in patients with cystic fibrosis, highlighting the need for specialized care and management tailored to this specific patient population."}{"title": "SAN FRANCISCO:San Francisco is a city in California where the DDW event took place in 2002, focusing on liver disease research."}{"title": "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF NUTRITION:The American College of Nutrition is a professional organization that focuses on the study and application of nutrition science."}{"title": "BRANCHED-CHAIN AMINO ACIDS:Branched-chain amino acids are essential nutrients that the body obtains from proteins found in food, often used in nutritional supplementation for liver disease."}{"title": "HOSPITAL VIRGEN DE LA VICTORIA:Hospital Virgen de la Victoria is a clinical hospital specializing in endocrinology and clinical nutrition located in M\u00e1laga, Spain."}{"title": "HOSPITAL QUIR\u00d3N-SALUD:Hospital Quir\u00f3n-salud is a clinical hospital specializing in endocrinology and clinical nutrition located in M\u00e1laga, Spain."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STATE:Nutritional state refers to the condition of the body in relation to the intake and utilization of nutrients, which can be affected by various health conditions, including liver diseases."}{"title": "POST-LIVER TRANSPLANTATION SARCOPENIA:Post-liver transplantation sarcopenia is a condition characterized by loss of muscle mass and strength following liver transplantation, often evaluated in patients with liver cirrhosis."}{"title": "ARETAEUS DE CAPADOCIA:Aretaeus de Capadocia was a physician in the second half of the 2nd century BC who first described the condition known as celiac disease."}{"title": "SAMUEL GEE:Samuel Gee was a physician who provided a more contemporary clinical report on celiac disease in 1888, emphasizing the importance of dietary regulation in treatment."}{"title": "GLUTEN DICKE:Gluten Dicke was a researcher who made a significant discovery regarding the relationship between gluten consumption and celiac disease after World War II."}{"title": "HLA DQ2:HLA DQ2 is a genetic marker associated with a higher predisposition to celiac disease and related conditions."}{"title": "HLA DQ8:HLA DQ8 is another genetic marker linked to an increased risk of developing celiac disease."}{"title": "MINERALS:Minerals are inorganic elements that are essential for human health and play a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are commonly found in dietary supplements and are vital for maintaining overall well-being. Additionally, the absorption of these inorganic nutrients can be impaired in individuals with celiac disease, highlighting the importance of understanding mineral intake and its impact on health."}{"title": "HYPERPLASIA:Hyperplasia is an increase in the number of cells, which can occur in the intestinal mucosa of individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "ATROPHY:Atrophy refers to the wasting away or decrease in size of the intestinal villi, a characteristic of celiac disease."}{"title": "IMMUNE RESPONSE:The immune response is the body's reaction to gluten in individuals with celiac disease, leading to inflammation and damage."}{"title": "LYMPHOCYTES:Lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell involved in the immune response, which plays a role in the pathology of celiac disease."}{"title": "ANTIGLIADIN ANTIBODIES:Antigliadin antibodies are markers that can indicate an autoimmune response to gluten in individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "ANTIENDOMYSIAL ANTIBODIES:Antiendomysial antibodies are another type of antibody that can be present in individuals with celiac disease, indicating intestinal damage."}{"title": "ANTIRETICULIN ANTIBODIES:Antireticulin antibodies are associated with celiac disease and can be used as a diagnostic marker for the condition."}{"title": "GLUTEN SENSITIVITY:Gluten sensitivity is a condition characterized by individuals experiencing symptoms related to gluten consumption. It is distinct from celiac disease, meaning that those with gluten sensitivity do not have the autoimmune response associated with celiac disease."}{"title": "ICEBERG CELIAC:The iceberg celiac theory suggests that many individuals with celiac disease may remain undiagnosed, with only a small percentage showing classic symptoms.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CEREAL:Cereal is a type of grain that is rich in carbohydrates and includes various species consumed by humans such as wheat, barley, and corn."}{"title": "HARINA DE CEREAL:Flour made from cereal grains, primarily used in baking and cooking."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA:SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA, or non-celiac gluten sensitivity, is a condition characterized by gastrointestinal symptoms that occur in response to gluten consumption. Unlike celiac disease, individuals with this sensitivity do not exhibit the same diagnostic markers associated with celiac disease. This distinction highlights that while both conditions involve adverse reactions to gluten, they are fundamentally different in their underlying mechanisms and diagnostic criteria."}{"title": "CORN:Corn is a cereal grain that is widely used in various food products and is gluten-free."}{"title": "BARLEY:Barley is a cereal grain that contains gluten and can trigger symptoms in individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "VITAMINAS DEL GRUPO B:B vitamins are a group of water-soluble vitamins that play important roles in cell metabolism and are found in various cereals."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS EXTRAINTENSTINALES:Extraintestinal symptoms are non-digestive reactions that can occur in individuals with celiac disease, such as fatigue and headaches."}{"title": "DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN:The \"DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN\" refers to a gluten-free diet, which is a dietary regimen that excludes foods containing gluten. This diet is primarily adopted by individuals diagnosed with celiac disease or those who experience gluten sensitivity. Research has shown that a gluten-free diet can also be beneficial for some patients suffering from irritable bowel syndrome and gluten sensitivity, as indicated by clinical trials. It is particularly recommended for patients with celiac disease to help manage and control the symptoms associated with this condition."}{"title": "HUMANO:HUMANO refers to humans, who are classified as primates. One notable characteristic of humans is the absence of the enzyme uricase, which results in elevated levels of uric acid in their bodies compared to other mammals. Additionally, humans are susceptible to celiac disease and gluten sensitivity, conditions that can trigger a range of symptoms when gluten is consumed."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS 1:La diabetes mellitus tipo 1 es una enfermedad autoinmune que se ha asociado con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, presentando un riesgo mayor en pacientes cel\u00edacos."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE SJ\u00d6GREN:La enfermedad de Sj\u00f6gren es otra patolog\u00eda autoinmune que puede estar asociada con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "INFERTILIDAD:La infertilidad puede ser una complicaci\u00f3n en pacientes con enfermedad cel\u00edaca, a menudo relacionada con deficiencias nutricionales."}{"title": "ABORTOS:Los abortos de repetici\u00f3n pueden estar asociados con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, debido a problemas de malnutrici\u00f3n y autoinmunidad."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS NEUROPSIQUI\u00c1TRICOS:Los trastornos neuropsiqui\u00e1tricos son manifestaciones que pueden asociarse con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, incluyendo ataxia, cefaleas y trastornos ansioso-depresivos."}{"title": "ARTRITIS:Artritis es una condici\u00f3n que puede aparecer en un porcentaje significativo de adultos que padecen enfermedad cel\u00edaca, lo que sugiere una relaci\u00f3n entre ambas condiciones."}{"title": "DERMATITIS HERPETIFORME:Dermatitis herpetiforme es una erupci\u00f3n cut\u00e1nea que se asocia con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca. Esta condici\u00f3n se manifiesta a trav\u00e9s de lesiones ves\u00edculo-papulosas y pruriginosas, afectando de manera sim\u00e9trica las extremidades y la regi\u00f3n gl\u00fatea."}{"title": "SINDROME DE DOWN:El s\u00edndrome de Down es una condici\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica que se ha asociado con un riesgo significativamente mayor de desarrollar enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD TIROIDEA:Los trastornos tiroideos autoinmunes, como el hipotiroidismo, son m\u00e1s frecuentes en pacientes con enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD HEPATICA:La enfermedad hep\u00e1tica puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad cel\u00edaca, incluyendo hepatitis autoinmune y cirrosis biliar primaria."}{"title": "MIOCARDITIS Y MIOCARDIOPATIA DILATADA:La miocarditis y la miocardiopat\u00eda dilatada son condiciones card\u00edacas que pueden asociarse raramente con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "HIPOESPLENISMO:El hipoesplenismo es una condici\u00f3n que se ha descrito en casos asociados a la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, aumentando el riesgo de infecciones severas."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT SELECTIVO DE IGA:El d\u00e9ficit selectivo de IgA aparece en un 1-2% de los pacientes cel\u00edacos, lo que indica una posible relaci\u00f3n con la enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "RIESGO DE NEOPLASIAS:El riesgo de aparici\u00f3n de ciertos tumores, como linfoma intestinal no-Hodgkin, parece estar aumentado en pacientes con enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES EN LAS FANERAS:Las alteraciones en las faneras, como piel, pelo y u\u00f1as, pueden ser s\u00edntomas de deficiencias nutricionales en pacientes cel\u00edacos."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DOWN:Trastorno gen\u00e9tico que puede estar asociado a un mayor riesgo de enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE WILLIAMS:Trastorno gen\u00e9tico que puede estar asociado a un mayor riesgo de enfermedad cel\u00edaca."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGA ANTIENDOMISIO:Prueba serol\u00f3gica utilizada para el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, con alta sensibilidad y especificidad."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGA ANTITRANSGLUTAMINASA:Prueba serol\u00f3gica utilizada para el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, con alta sensibilidad y especificidad."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGA ANTIGLIADINA:Prueba serol\u00f3gica utilizada para el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, con sensibilidad y especificidad moderadas."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS IGG ANTIGLIADINA:Prueba serol\u00f3gica utilizada para el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, con sensibilidad y especificidad moderadas."}{"title": "PACIENTES CELIACOS:"}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS EMA:Los anticuerpos EMA son marcadores serol\u00f3gicos utilizados en el diagn\u00f3stico de la enfermedad cel\u00edaca, indicando la presencia de una respuesta inmune al gluten."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS TTG:Los anticuerpos antitransglutaminasa (tTG) son pruebas serol\u00f3gicas que ayudan a diagnosticar la enfermedad cel\u00edaca al detectar la respuesta inmune al gluten."}{"title": "D-XILOSA:La D-xilosa es un monosac\u00e1rido utilizado en pruebas para evaluar la absorci\u00f3n intestinal y la integridad de la mucosa intestinal en el diagn\u00f3stico de malabsorci\u00f3n."}{"title": "DIETISTA:A dietitian is a healthcare professional who specializes in nutrition and diet planning, particularly for patients with specific dietary needs. This expertise is especially crucial for individuals with conditions such as celiac disease, as a specialized dietitian can tailor dietary recommendations to meet their unique requirements."}{"title": "CEBADA:La cebada es otro cereal que contiene gluten y es perjudicial para los pacientes con celiaqu\u00eda."}{"title": "AMARANTO:El amaranto es un cereal sin gluten que se puede consumir de forma segura por los pacientes con celiaqu\u00eda."}{"title": "MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM:Un equipo multidisciplinario que proporciona seguimiento continuo a pacientes con enfermedad celiaca para supervisar la efectividad del tratamiento."}{"title": "CALORIC REQUIREMENTS:Requerimientos cal\u00f3ricos que deben ser calculados y adaptados a las necesidades individuales de los pacientes con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "DIETARY HABITS:Dietary habits refer to the patterns of food consumption that can significantly impact health outcomes, including cardiovascular health. These habits encompass various aspects of an individual's diet, including the types of foods consumed and the frequency of consumption. Additionally, it is important to consider the previous dietary habits of patients, particularly when adapting to specific dietary requirements, such as following a gluten-free diet. Respecting and adapting these prior habits is crucial for ensuring compliance and promoting overall health in individuals making dietary changes."}{"title": "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD DE ESPA\u00d1A:The Ministry of Health of Spain oversees public health policies and provides guidelines regarding celiac disease and gluten-free diets."}{"title": "CELIAC SPRUE ASSOCIATION:The Celiac Sprue Association is a U.S.-based organization that provides support and resources for individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF DIABETES AND DIGESTIVE AND KIDNEY DISEASES:The National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) is a component of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) that focuses on conducting research and disseminating information related to various health issues. This institute is dedicated to studying digestive diseases, including celiac disease, and also provides valuable information on lactose intolerance. Through its research initiatives and educational resources, the NIDDK aims to enhance understanding and treatment of conditions affecting diabetes, digestive health, and kidney function."}{"title": "GLUTEN INTOLERANCE GROUP:The Gluten Intolerance Group is an organization that offers support and resources for individuals with gluten-related disorders."}{"title": "SCOTT ADAMS ASSOCIATION:An association that supports individuals with celiac disease and promotes awareness about gluten-free diets."}{"title": "EUROPEAN COELIAC SOCIETIES:An association that represents various organizations across Europe focused on celiac disease and gluten-free living."}{"title": "GLUTEN-FREE DIET:The gluten-free diet is a dietary regimen that excludes gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. This diet is essential for managing celiac disease and gluten intolerance, as it helps individuals avoid the adverse health effects associated with the consumption of gluten."}{"title": "HARINA DE MA\u00cdZ:Corn flour is a gluten-free alternative to wheat flour that can be used in various recipes."}{"title": "HARINA DE PATATAS:Potato flour is another gluten-free substitute that can be used in cooking and baking."}{"title": "HARINA DE ARROZ:Rice flour is a gluten-free flour option that is often used in gluten-free recipes."}{"title": "ALMID\u00d3N DE PATATA:Potato starch is a gluten-free thickening agent that can be used in cooking."}{"title": "HARINA DE SOJA:Soy flour is a gluten-free alternative that is high in protein and can be used in various recipes."}{"title": "HARINA DE TRIGO:"}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA EN GLUTEN:The \"DIETA CONTROLADA EN GLUTEN\" is a dietary regimen that excludes foods containing gluten. This diet is primarily recommended for individuals with celiac disease, a condition that necessitates strict avoidance of gluten to prevent adverse health effects. It is utilized mainly by those diagnosed with this condition to manage their symptoms and maintain overall health."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS SIN GLUTEN:\"ALIMENTOS SIN GLUTEN\" refers to foods that do not contain gluten, making them safe for consumption by individuals with celiac disease. These gluten-free foods are specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of those who cannot tolerate gluten, ensuring their health and well-being."}{"title": "HARINAS DE TRIGO:Las harinas de trigo son un ingrediente b\u00e1sico en muchos productos de panader\u00eda y contienen gluten, lo que las hace inapropiadas para personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "BOLLOS:Los bollos son productos de pasteler\u00eda que generalmente contienen gluten y deben ser evitados por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "PASTAS ITALIANAS:Las pastas italianas, como fideos y macarrones, son alimentos que contienen gluten y deben ser evitados por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "LECHE Y DERIVADOS:La leche y sus derivados son alimentos que no contienen gluten y son seguros para el consumo de personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "QUESOS FUNDIDOS:Los quesos fundidos de sabores pueden contener gluten y deben ser verificados antes de su consumo por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "PAT\u00c9S:Los pat\u00e9s diversos pueden contener gluten y deben ser consumidos con precauci\u00f3n por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "CONSERVAS DE CARNES:Las conservas de carnes pueden contener gluten y deben ser verificadas por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "CONSERVAS DE PESCADOS:Las conservas de pescados con distintas salsas pueden contener gluten y deben ser consumidas con precauci\u00f3n por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "SUCED\u00c1NEOS DE CAF\u00c9:Los suced\u00e1neos de caf\u00e9 y otras bebidas de m\u00e1quina pueden contener gluten y deben ser verificados antes de su consumo por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "FRUTOS SECOS TOSTADOS:Los frutos secos tostados con sal pueden contener gluten y deben ser consumidos con precauci\u00f3n por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "SUCED\u00c1NEOS DE CHOCOLATE:Los suced\u00e1neos de chocolate pueden contener gluten y deben ser verificados antes de su consumo por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "COLORANTE ALIMENTARIO:El colorante alimentario puede contener gluten y debe ser verificado antes de su uso por personas con enfermedad celiaca."}{"title": "GLUTEN-FREE CERTIFICATION ORGANIZATION:The Gluten-Free Certification Organization is an entity established to certify food products as gluten-free, adhering to stringent criteria. Its primary mission is to provide certification for gluten-free products, ensuring safety and reliability for individuals with celiac disease and other gluten-related disorders."}{"title": "CODIGO ALIMENTARIO:The Codex Alimentarius is a collection of internationally recognized standards, guidelines, and codes of practice to ensure food safety and quality."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS Y AMINO\u00c1CIDOS:Prote\u00ednas y Amino\u00e1cidos is a section discussing the content of gluten in various food groups, particularly focusing on proteins and amino acids."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RECOMENDADOS:Alimentos recomendados refers to food items that do not contain gluten and are safe for individuals with celiac disease."}{"title": "FARIN\u00c1CEOS:Farin\u00e1ceos refers to a group of food items, including bread and cereals, that are typically high in gluten and should be avoided."}{"title": "TUB\u00c9RCULOS Y DERIVADOS:Tub\u00e9rculos y derivados refers to food items that can replace gluten-containing cereals in a diet.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "BONIATOS:Los boniatos son un tipo de tub\u00e9rculo recomendado en la dieta controlada en gluten, preferidos en su forma fresca."}{"title": "PATATAS RELLENAS:Las patatas rellenas de ketchup y/o mostaza son un alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten."}{"title": "PUR\u00c9 DE PATATA INSTANT\u00c1NEO:El pur\u00e9 de patata instant\u00e1neo es un alimento que puede ser consumido en la dieta controlada en gluten si se elige la versi\u00f3n adecuada."}{"title": "CARNES EN CONSERVA:Las carnes en conserva son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que pueden contener gluten."}{"title": "PESCADOS REBOZADOS:Los pescados rebozados son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que contienen gluten."}{"title": "SUCED\u00c1NEOS DE MARISCO:Los suced\u00e1neos de marisco son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten, ya que pueden contener gluten."}{"title": "CONSERVAS DE PESCADO:Las conservas de pescado en salsa o con tomate son un tipo de alimento a evitar en la dieta controlada en gluten."}Ø0␀␀␀␀␀áØ0␀␀␀␀␀ÙØ0␀␀␀␀␀w∞0␀␀␀␀␀‰∞0␀␀␀␀␀T±0␀␀␀␀␀ÿ±0␀␀␀␀␀I≤0␀␀␀␀␀¬≤0␀␀␀␀␀@≥0␀␀␀␀␀∂≥0␀␀␀␀␀/¥0␀␀␀␀␀ô¥0␀␀␀␀␀µ0␀␀␀␀␀ôµ0␀␀␀␀␀∂0␀␀␀␀␀m∂0␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ∂0␀␀␀␀␀I∑0␀␀␀␀␀µ∑0␀␀␀␀␀∏0␀␀␀␀␀ì∏0␀␀␀␀␀˚∏0␀␀␀␀␀Yπ0␀␀␀␀␀¡π0␀␀␀␀␀"∫0␀␀␀␀␀Ä∫0␀␀␀␀␀˚∫0␀␀␀␀␀iª0␀␀␀␀␀“ª0␀␀␀␀␀3º0␀␀␀␀␀•º0␀␀␀␀␀!Ω0␀␀␀␀␀äΩ0␀␀␀␀␀±ø0␀␀␀␀␀N¿0␀␀␀␀␀˙¿0␀␀␀␀␀£¡0␀␀␀␀␀A¬0␀␀␀␀␀Ú√0␀␀␀␀␀£ƒ0␀␀␀␀␀>≈0␀␀␀␀␀∑≈0␀␀␀␀␀f∆0␀␀␀␀␀◊∆0␀␀␀␀␀Ü«0␀␀␀␀␀%»0␀␀␀␀␀Ù»0␀␀␀␀␀Î 0␀␀␀␀␀ôÃ0␀␀␀␀␀OÕ0␀␀␀␀␀ËÕ0␀␀␀␀␀õŒ0␀␀␀␀␀:œ0␀␀␀␀␀?—0␀␀␀␀␀Œ“0␀␀␀␀␀õ‘0␀␀␀␀␀÷0␀␀␀␀␀∫◊0␀␀␀␀␀ÑŸ0␀␀␀␀␀1⁄0␀␀␀␀␀Ç€0␀␀␀␀␀H‹0␀␀␀␀␀`‡0␀␀␀␀␀·0␀␀␀␀␀C·0␀␀␀␀␀E‚0␀␀␀␀␀␀„0␀␀␀␀␀û„0␀␀␀␀␀Ê0␀␀␀␀␀&Ê0␀␀␀␀␀1È0␀␀␀␀␀Í0␀␀␀␀␀ØÏ0␀␀␀␀␀sÌ0␀␀␀␀␀Ò0␀␀␀␀␀¸Ò0␀␀␀␀␀≠Ú0␀␀␀␀␀wÛ0␀␀␀␀␀Ù0␀␀␀␀␀≠Ù0␀␀␀␀␀<ı0␀␀␀␀␀>ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀@¯0␀␀␀␀␀Ô¯0␀␀␀␀␀ã˘0␀␀␀␀␀„˙0␀␀␀␀␀¨˚0␀␀␀␀␀í˝0␀␀␀␀␀6ˇ0␀␀␀␀␀ıˇ0␀␀␀␀␀∏␀1␀␀␀␀␀n1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀´1␀␀␀␀␀71␀␀␀␀␀È1␀␀␀␀␀_1␀␀␀␀␀Ò1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀…1␀␀␀␀␀{1␀␀␀␀␀˜1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀¯	1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀r1␀␀␀␀␀|1␀␀␀␀␀\1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀≈1␀␀␀␀␀ê1␀␀␀␀␀61␀␀␀␀␀⁄1␀␀␀␀␀o1␀␀␀␀␀ˇ1␀␀␀␀␀ä1␀␀␀␀␀-1␀␀␀␀␀E1␀␀␀␀␀%1␀␀␀␀␀g1␀␀␀␀␀:1␀␀␀␀␀ˆ1␀␀␀␀␀•1␀␀␀␀␀p1␀␀␀␀␀: 1␀␀␀␀␀Í 1␀␀␀␀␀µ!1␀␀␀␀␀l"1␀␀␀␀␀!#1␀␀␀␀␀⁄#1␀␀␀␀␀ó$1␀␀␀␀␀m%1␀␀␀␀␀&1␀␀␀␀␀§&1␀␀␀␀␀\'1␀␀␀␀␀(1␀␀␀␀␀Ø(1␀␀␀␀␀@)1␀␀␀␀␀∆)1␀␀␀␀␀T*1␀␀␀␀␀˚*1␀␀␀␀␀ü+1␀␀␀␀␀-1␀␀␀␀␀k/1␀␀␀␀␀01␀␀␀␀␀“01␀␀␀␀␀11␀␀␀␀␀®21␀␀␀␀␀ø41␀␀␀␀␀÷41␀␀␀␀␀¨51␀␀␀␀␀R71␀␀␀␀␀81␀␀␀␀␀=:1␀␀␀␀␀;1␀␀␀